This is a great idea. Keeping the validation logic and user experience identical across the JournalPosting.js (Maker) and JournalAuthorization.js (Checker) screens is best practice for enterprise applications. It prevents confusion and guarantees clean data at every step.
We will introduce the exact same filterAndWarn engine into the Authorization screen to provide real-time Snackbar warnings and strictly format the strings.
Here are the precise replacements to make in **JournalAuthorization.js**.
### 1. Add the Validation and Warning Engine
Find the old handleRemarksChange and isRemarksValid definitions (around line 125).
**Find this block:**
```javascript
  // Professional character filtering: only allow a-z, A-Z, 0-9 and space
  const handleRemarksChange = (e, setter) => {
    const value = e.target.value;
    const filteredValue = value.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9 ]/g, "");
    setter(filteredValue);
  };

  // Validation logic: Remarks are compulsory (min 2, max 30)
  const isRemarksValid = (val) => val.trim().length >= 2 && val.trim().length <= 30;

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
  // Real-time filter & Snackbar Warning Engine
  const filterAndWarn = (val, type) => {
    let filtered = val;
    let hasError = false;
    let msg = "Only alphabets and digits are allowed.";

    if (type === "alphanumeric_space") {
      filtered = val.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9 ]/g, ""); // Strip special chars
      if (filtered !== val) {
        hasError = true;
      }
      
      // Strip leading space and collapse double spaces
      const beforeSpaceTrim = filtered;
      filtered = filtered.replace(/^\s+/, "").replace(/\s{2,}/g, " ");
      if (beforeSpaceTrim !== filtered && !hasError) {
        hasError = true;
        msg = "Leading or multiple spaces are not allowed.";
      }
    }

    if (hasError) {
      showSnackBar(msg, "warning");
    }
    return filtered;
  };

  const handleRemarksChange = (e, setter) => {
    const val = filterAndWarn(e.target.value, "alphanumeric_space");
    if (val.length <= 30) {
      setter(val);
    }
  };

  // Validation logic: Remarks are strictly compulsory (min 2, max 30)
  const isRemarksValid = (val) => val.trim().length >= 2 && val.trim().length <= 30;

```
